    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before becoming Stannards, the hamlet was originally called Stannards Corners, reflecting its early crossroads layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stannards%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Wellsville, Cuba & Pennsylvania Railroad ran through Stannards, linking local farmers to wider markets for dairy and maple syrup.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/stannards_new_york"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Genesee River winds northward through Stannards, providing a natural corridor that shaped early settlement patterns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stannards%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Around 1900, Stannards boasted a hotel, store, post office, blacksmith shop, Methodist Episcopal Church, parsonage, and school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
